  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Dayashankar vs State Of M.P. on 16 November, 2017 1 Criminal Revision No.628/1999 [Dayashankar Vs. State of M.P.] High Court Of Madhya Pradesh Principal Seat Jabalpur Single Bench: Hon. Shri Justice G.S. Ahluwalia Criminal Revision No.628/1999 .........Applicant: Dayashankar Versus .........Respondent: State of M.P. Shri Anand Nayak, Counsel for the applicant. Shri Manish Awasthy, Public Prosecutor for respondent/State. ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- Date of hearing : 16/11/2017 Date of order : 16/11/2017 Whether approved for reporting : Order",
    "facts": "The necessary facts for the disposal of the present criminal revision in short are that on 29-9-1991, at about 9 A.M., the Food Inspector purchased 750 M.L. of milk from the applicant, who was the Milk Vendor. The purchased milk was distributed and was 2 Criminal Revision No.628/1999 [Dayashankar Vs. State of M.P.] kept equally in three different dry and clean glass bottles. 20 drops of formalin were added in each bottle. The sample was sent to Public Analyst. The report of the Public Analyst was received on 7-11-1991 and after obtaining necessary sanction for prosecution, the complaint was filed on 10-1-1992. A singular submission was made by the Counsel for the applicant that since the complaint was not filed immediately after the receipt of the report of the Public Analyst, therefore, the valuable right of the accused under Section 13(2) of Prevention of Food Adulteration Act (In short the Act) was infringed. Dayashankar vs State Of M.P. on 16 November, 2017 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/86667309/ 1 It is clear that the samples were collected on 29-9- 1991. The complaint was filed on 10-1-1992. The copy of the report of the Public Analyst was sent to the applicant by registered post on 24-1-1992. However, the applicant did not file any application under Section 13(2) of Act for getting the second sample re-examined by Central Food Laboratory. The samples were collected on 29-9-1991 and the complaint was filed on 10-1-1992 and the copy of the report of the Public Analyst 3 Criminal Revision No.628/1999 [Dayashankar Vs. State of M.P.] was sent on 24-1-1992.",
    "arguments": "This Court in the case of Mohd. Baitulla Vs. State of M.P. reported in ILR (2011) MP 2607 has held as under : 16.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "This Court in the case of Mohd. Baitulla Vs. State of M.P. reported in ILR (2011) MP 2607 has held as under : 16."
  },
